(window.DSA_TOPIC=window.DSA_TOPIC||{})["linked-list"]={"id":"linked-list","theory":"\n<h3>What it is</h3>\n<p>A <b>linked list</b> is a chain of nodes; each node holds a value and a pointer to the <code>next</code> node. There's no index: reaching the k-th node takes k steps. In exchange, inserting or removing a node you already hold is O(1) — you just re-point arrows.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">class ListNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, next=None):\n        self.val, self.next = val, next</code></pre>\n<h3>Costs</h3>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Operation</th><th>Linked list</th><th>Array</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Access k-th element</td><td>O(k)</td><td>O(1)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Insert / delete after a known node</td><td>O(1)</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Insert at head</td><td>O(1)</td><td>O(n)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3>The five techniques</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Dummy head</b> — <code>dummy = ListNode(0, head)</code> removes special cases when the head itself might change (merge, delete, partition).</li>\n<li><b>Fast &amp; slow pointers</b> — fast moves 2, slow moves 1. Finds the middle, detects cycles (they meet), and finds the cycle start.</li>\n<li><b>Gap pointers</b> — move one pointer n steps ahead, then move both: the slow one stops n from the end.</li>\n<li><b>In-place reversal</b> — <code>prev, cur = None, head</code>; repeatedly flip <code>cur.next</code> to <code>prev</code>.</li>\n<li><b>Split &amp; merge</b> — find the middle, reverse or sort the halves, weave them together (reorder list, palindrome, merge sort).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Template: reverse</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">prev, cur = None, head\nwhile cur:\n    nxt = cur.next     # 1. save the rest\n    cur.next = prev    # 2. flip the arrow\n    prev, cur = cur, nxt  # 3. step forward\nreturn prev</code></pre>\n<h3>Common mistakes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Losing the rest of the list by overwriting <code>cur.next</code> before saving it.</li>\n<li>Checking <code>fast.next.next</code> without first checking <code>fast</code> and <code>fast.next</code>.</li>\n<li>Forgetting to cut the tail (<code>tail.next = None</code>) after rearranging, creating an accidental cycle.</li>\n</ul>\n","qs":{"reverse-linked-list":{"statement":"Reverse a singly linked list and return the new head.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","[5, 4, 3, 2, 1]"],["head = [1, 2]","[2, 1]"],["head = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Copy the values into an array and build a new list from the back.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def reverse_list(head):\n    vals = []\n    while head:\n        vals.append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    dummy = cur = ListNode()\n    for v in reversed(vals):\n        cur.next = ListNode(v)\n        cur = cur.next\n    return dummy.next"},"opt":{"idea":"Walk the list once with prev / cur and point each node back at prev.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def reverse_list(head):\n    prev, cur = None, head\n    while cur:\n        nxt = cur.next\n        cur.next = prev\n        prev, cur = cur, nxt\n    return prev","frames":[{"m":"Node 1 now points back; move on","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"remaining","v":["2","3","4","5"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed","v":["1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Node 2 now points back; move on","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"remaining","v":["3","4","5"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed","v":["2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Node 3 now points back; move on","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"remaining","v":["4","5"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed","v":["3","2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Node 4 now points back; move on","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"remaining","v":["5"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed","v":["4","3","2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Node 5 now points back; move on","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"remaining","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed","v":["5","4","3","2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"remaining","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed","v":["5","4","3","2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"merge-two-sorted-lists":{"statement":"Merge two sorted linked lists into one sorted list by splicing their nodes.","examples":[["l1 = [1, 2, 4], l2 = [1, 3, 4]","[1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4]"],["l1 = [], l2 = []","[]"],["l1 = [], l2 = [0]","[0]"]],"vizIn":"l1 = [1, 2, 4], l2 = [1, 3, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Collect all values, sort them, build a new list.","tc":"O((m+n) log(m+n))","sc":"O(m + n)","code":"def merge_two_lists(l1, l2):\n    vals = []\n    for node in (l1, l2):\n        while node:\n            vals.append(node.val)\n            node = node.next\n    dummy = cur = ListNode()\n    for v in sorted(vals):\n        cur.next = ListNode(v)\n        cur = cur.next\n    return dummy.next"},"opt":{"idea":"A dummy node and a tail pointer. Attach the smaller head each step; when one list runs out, attach the rest of the other.","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def merge_two_lists(l1, l2):\n    dummy = tail = ListNode()\n    while l1 and l2:\n        if l1.val <= l2.val:\n            tail.next, l1 = l1, l1.next\n        else:\n            tail.next, l2 = l2, l2.next\n        tail = tail.next\n    tail.next = l1 or l2\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"Attach 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","2","4"],"p":{"tail":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["2","4"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["1","3","4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Attach 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","3","4"],"p":{"tail":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["2","4"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["3","4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Attach 2","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","4"],"p":{"tail":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["4"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["3","4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Attach 3","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4"],"p":{"tail":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["4"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Attach 4","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4"],"p":{"tail":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4"],"p":{"tail":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"linked-list-cycle":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if the list has a cycle (some node's next points back to an earlier node).","examples":[["head = [3, 2, 0, -4], pos = 1","True"],["head = [1, 2], pos = 0","True"],["head = [1], pos = -1","False"]],"vizIn":"head = [3, 2, 0, -4], pos = 1","brute":{"idea":"Store every visited node in a set; a repeat means a cycle.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def has_cycle(head):\n    seen = set()\n    while head:\n        if head in seen:\n            return True\n        seen.add(head)\n        head = head.next\n    return False"},"opt":{"idea":"Floyd: slow moves 1, fast moves 2. If there's a cycle fast laps slow and they meet; otherwise fast hits None.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def has_cycle(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n        if slow is fast:\n            return True\n    return False","frames":[{"m":"slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","0","-4"],"p":{"slow":1,"fast":2},"cyc":1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","0","-4"],"p":{"slow":2,"fast":1},"cyc":1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","0","-4"],"p":{"slow":3,"fast":3},"cyc":1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"They met → cycle","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","0","-4"],"p":{"slow":3,"fast":3},"cyc":1,"hl":[3]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","0","-4"],"p":{"slow":3,"fast":3},"cyc":1,"hl":[3]}]}]},"tests":3},"linked-list-cycle-ii":{"statement":"Return the node where the cycle begins, or <code>None</code>. (The answer shown is that node's value.)","examples":[["head = [3, 2, 0, -4], pos = 1","2"],["head = [1, 2], pos = 0","1"],["head = [1], pos = -1","None"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], pos = 2","brute":{"idea":"Walk with a set; the first node seen twice is the entrance.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def detect_cycle(head):\n    seen = set()\n    while head:\n        if head in seen:\n            return head\n        seen.add(head)\n        head = head.next\n    return None"},"opt":{"idea":"After slow and fast meet, restart one pointer at head and move both by 1. The distance math (a = k·c − b) makes them meet exactly at the cycle entrance.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def detect_cycle(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n        if slow is fast:\n            break\n    else:\n        return None\n    p = head\n    while p is not slow:\n        p, slow = p.next, slow.next\n    return p","frames":[{"m":"Phase 1: slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":1,"fast":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Phase 1: slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":2,"fast":4},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Phase 1: slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":3,"fast":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Phase 1: slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":4,"fast":4},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Phase 2: from head and from the meeting point, both +1","l":10,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"p":1,"slow":5},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Phase 2: from head and from the meeting point, both +1","l":10,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"p":2,"slow":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"They meet at 3: the cycle entrance","l":11,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"entrance":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[2]}]},{"m":"Result: 3","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"entrance":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[2]}]}]},"tests":3},"middle-of-the-linked-list":{"statement":"Return the middle node (the second middle if there are two). Shown as the list from that node.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","[3, 4, 5]"],["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]","[4, 5, 6]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Count the length, then walk length // 2 steps.","tc":"O(n) — two passes","sc":"O(1)","code":"def middle_node(head):\n    n, cur = 0, head\n    while cur:\n        n, cur = n + 1, cur.next\n    for _ in range(n // 2):\n        head = head.next\n    return head"},"opt":{"idea":"When fast (2 steps) reaches the end, slow (1 step) is in the middle.","tc":"O(n) — one pass","sc":"O(1)","code":"def middle_node(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n    return slow","frames":[{"m":"Both start at head","l":2,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":0,"fast":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":1,"fast":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow +1, fast +2","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":2,"fast":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [3, 4, 5]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":2,"fast":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":2},"remove-nth-node-from-end-of-list":{"statement":"Remove the n-th node from the end and return the head.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], n = 2","[1, 2, 3, 5]"],["head = [1], n = 1","[]"],["head = [1, 2], n = 1","[1]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], n = 2","brute":{"idea":"Count the length L, then remove node L − n from the front.","tc":"O(n) — two passes","sc":"O(1)","code":"def remove_nth_from_end(head, n):\n    length, cur = 0, head\n    while cur:\n        length, cur = length + 1, cur.next\n    dummy = ListNode(0, head)\n    cur = dummy\n    for _ in range(length - n):\n        cur = cur.next\n    cur.next = cur.next.next\n    return dummy.next"},"opt":{"idea":"Move fast n steps ahead of slow (both start at a dummy). Move both until fast is at the last node; slow.next is the node to delete.","tc":"O(n) — one pass","sc":"O(1)","code":"def remove_nth_from_end(head, n):\n    dummy = ListNode(0, head)\n    slow = fast = dummy\n    for _ in range(n):\n        fast = fast.next\n    while fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next\n    slow.next = slow.next.next\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"fast is 2 node(s) ahead of slow","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":0,"fast":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Move both by one","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":1,"fast":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Move both by one","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":2,"fast":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Move both by one","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":3,"fast":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow.next (4) is n-th from the end → skip it","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[4]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, 5]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"slow":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[4]}]}]},"tests":3},"reorder-list":{"statement":"Reorder L0 → L1 → … → Ln into L0 → Ln → L1 → Ln−1 → … in place.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4]","[1, 4, 2, 3]"],["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","[1, 5, 2, 4, 3]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Put the nodes in an array and relink them with two indices from both ends.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def reorder_list(head):\n    nodes = []\n    while head:\n        nodes.append(head)\n        head = head.next\n    i, j = 0, len(nodes) - 1\n    while i < j:\n        nodes[i].next = nodes[j]\n        i += 1\n        if i == j:\n            break\n        nodes[j].next = nodes[i]\n        j -= 1\n    nodes[i].next = None"},"opt":{"idea":"Find the middle, reverse the second half, then alternately take a node from each half.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def reorder_list(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast.next and fast.next.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n    second, slow.next = slow.next, None\n    prev = None\n    while second:\n        second.next, prev, second = prev, second, second.next\n    second = prev\n    first = head\n    while second:\n        n1, n2 = first.next, second.next\n        first.next, second.next = second, n1\n        first, second = n1, n2","frames":[{"m":"1) Split at the middle","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"first half","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"second half","v":["3","4"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"2) Reverse the second half","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"first half","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"second half","v":["4","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"3) Weave one node from each half","l":13,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"result","v":["1","4","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[2]},{"k":"list","n":"left in second half","v":["3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"3) Weave one node from each half","l":13,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"result","v":["1","4","2","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"left in second half","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 4, 2, 3]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"result","v":["1","4","2","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"left in second half","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":2},"palindrome-linked-list":{"statement":"Return <code>True</code> if the list's values read the same forwards and backwards.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 2, 1]","True"],["head = [1, 2]","False"],["head = [1, 2, 3, 2, 1]","True"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 1]","brute":{"idea":"Copy values to an array and compare it with its reverse.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def is_palindrome_list(head):\n    vals = []\n    while head:\n        vals.append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    return vals == vals[::-1]"},"opt":{"idea":"Find the middle, reverse the second half, compare the halves node by node.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def is_palindrome_list(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n    prev = None\n    while slow:\n        slow.next, prev, slow = prev, slow, slow.next\n    a, b = head, prev\n    while b:\n        if a.val != b.val:\n            return False\n        a, b = a.next, b.next\n    return True","frames":[{"m":"Compare 1 and 1","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"front","v":["1","2","3","3"],"p":{"a":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed back half","v":["1","2","3"],"p":{"b":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Compare 2 and 2","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"front","v":["1","2","3","3"],"p":{"a":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed back half","v":["1","2","3"],"p":{"b":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Compare 3 and 3","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"front","v":["1","2","3","3"],"p":{"a":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed back half","v":["1","2","3"],"p":{"b":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: True","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"front","v":["1","2","3","3"],"p":{"a":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed back half","v":["1","2","3"],"p":{"b":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"intersection-of-two-linked-lists":{"statement":"Two lists may merge into a shared tail. Return the first shared node (shown by value), or <code>None</code>.","examples":[["onlyA = [4, 1], onlyB = [5, 6, 1], shared = [8, 4, 5]","8"],["onlyA = [1, 9, 1], onlyB = [3], shared = [2, 4]","2"],["onlyA = [2, 6, 4], onlyB = [1, 5], shared = []","None"]],"vizIn":"onlyA = [4, 1], onlyB = [5, 6, 1], shared = [8, 4, 5]","brute":{"idea":"Put every node of A in a set, then walk B until a node is in the set.","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(m)","code":"def get_intersection_node(head_a, head_b):\n    seen = set()\n    while head_a:\n        seen.add(head_a)\n        head_a = head_a.next\n    while head_b:\n        if head_b in seen:\n            return head_b\n        head_b = head_b.next\n    return None"},"opt":{"idea":"Pointer a walks A then B; pointer b walks B then A. Both travel m + n steps, so they line up at the intersection (or both reach None).","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def get_intersection_node(head_a, head_b):\n    a, b = head_a, head_b\n    while a is not b:\n        a = a.next if a else head_b\n        b = b.next if b else head_a\n    return a","frames":[{"m":"a at 4, b at 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 1, b at 6","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 8, b at 1","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 4, b at 8","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 5, b at 4","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at None, b at 5","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 5, b at None","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 6, b at 4","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"a at 1, b at 1","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Same node: 8","l":5,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[2]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]},{"m":"Result: 8","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"A","v":["4","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"a":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[2]},{"k":"list","n":"B","v":["5","6","1","8","4","5"],"p":{"b":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]}]},"tests":3},"add-two-numbers":{"statement":"Two non-negative numbers are stored as lists of digits in reverse order. Return their sum as a list in the same format.","examples":[["l1 = [2, 4, 3], l2 = [5, 6, 4]","[7, 0, 8]"],["l1 = [0], l2 = [0]","[0]"],["l1 = [9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9, 9], l2 = [9, 9, 9, 9]","[8, 9, 9, 9, 0, 0, 0, 1]"]],"vizIn":"l1 = [2, 4, 3], l2 = [5, 6, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Convert both lists to integers, add, convert back. (Overflows in languages with fixed-size ints.)","tc":"O(m + n)","sc":"O(m + n)","code":"def add_two_numbers(l1, l2):\n    def to_int(node):\n        n, place = 0, 1\n        while node:\n            n += node.val * place\n            node, place = node.next, place * 10\n        return n\n    total = to_int(l1) + to_int(l2)\n    dummy = cur = ListNode()\n    for d in reversed(str(total)):\n        cur.next = ListNode(int(d))\n        cur = cur.next\n    return dummy.next"},"opt":{"idea":"Add digit by digit like on paper, carrying into the next node.","tc":"O(max(m, n))","sc":"O(1) extra","code":"def add_two_numbers(l1, l2):\n    dummy = tail = ListNode()\n    carry = 0\n    while l1 or l2 or carry:\n        total = (l1.val if l1 else 0) + (l2.val if l2 else 0) + carry\n        carry, digit = divmod(total, 10)\n        tail.next = ListNode(digit)\n        tail = tail.next\n        l1 = l1.next if l1 else None\n        l2 = l2.next if l2 else None\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"7 → write 7, carry 0","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["2","4","3"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["5","6","4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"sum","v":["7"],"p":{"tail":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"10 → write 0, carry 1","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["4","3"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["6","4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"sum","v":["7","0"],"p":{"tail":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"8 → write 8, carry 0","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["3"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"sum","v":["7","0","8"],"p":{"tail":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [7, 0, 8]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"l1","v":["3"],"p":{"l1":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"l2","v":["4"],"p":{"l2":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"sum","v":["7","0","8"],"p":{"tail":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"lru-cache":{"statement":"Design a cache of fixed <code>capacity</code> with O(1) <code>get</code> and <code>put</code>; when full, evict the least recently used key.","examples":[["LRUCache(2) → put(1, 1) → put(2, 2) → get(1) → put(3, 3) → get(2) → put(4, 4) → get(1) → get(3) → get(4)","[None, None, 1, None, -1, None, -1, 3, 4]"]],"vizIn":"LRUCache(2) → put(1, 1) → put(2, 2) → get(1) → put(3, 3) → get(2) → put(4, 4) → get(1) → get(3) → get(4)","brute":{"idea":"Keep a list of (key, value) in recency order; every get/put searches and moves items.","tc":"O(n) per op","sc":"O(n)","code":"class LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity):\n        self.cap, self.items = capacity, []  # most recent last\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        for i, (k, v) in enumerate(self.items):\n            if k == key:\n                self.items.append(self.items.pop(i))\n                return v\n        return -1\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        for i, (k, _) in enumerate(self.items):\n            if k == key:\n                self.items.pop(i)\n                break\n        self.items.append((key, value))\n        if len(self.items) > self.cap:\n            self.items.pop(0)"},"opt":{"idea":"A dict maps key → node in a doubly linked list ordered by recency. get moves the node to the front; put inserts at the front and evicts the node before the tail sentinel.","tc":"O(1) per op","sc":"O(capacity)","code":"class LRUCache:\n    class Node:\n        def __init__(self, key=0, val=0):\n            self.key, self.val, self.prev, self.next = key, val, None, None\n\n    def __init__(self, capacity):\n        self.cap, self.map = capacity, {}\n        self.head, self.tail = self.Node(), self.Node()  # sentinels\n        self.head.next, self.tail.prev = self.tail, self.head\n\n    def _remove(self, node):\n        node.prev.next, node.next.prev = node.next, node.prev\n\n    def _add_front(self, node):\n        node.prev, node.next = self.head, self.head.next\n        self.head.next.prev = node\n        self.head.next = node\n\n    def _order(self):\n        out, cur = [], self.head.next\n        while cur is not self.tail:\n            out.append(f\"{cur.key}:{cur.val}\")\n            cur = cur.next\n        return out\n\n    def get(self, key):\n        if key not in self.map:\n            return -1\n        node = self.map[key]\n        self._remove(node)\n        self._add_front(node)\n        return node.val\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        if key in self.map:\n            self._remove(self.map[key])\n        node = self.Node(key, value)\n        self.map[key] = node\n        self._add_front(node)\n        if len(self.map) > self.cap:\n            lru = self.tail.prev\n            self._remove(lru)\n            del self.map[lru.key]","frames":[{"m":"put(1, 1) at the front","l":42,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["1:1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["1","node"]],"hl":"1"}]},{"m":"put(2, 2) at the front","l":42,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["2:2","1:1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["1","node"],["2","node"]],"hl":"2"}]},{"m":"get(1) → 1; move it to the front","l":30,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["1:1","2:2"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["1","node"],["2","node"]],"hl":"1"}]},{"m":"Over capacity → evict least recent key 2","l":42,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["3:3","1:1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["1","node"],["3","node"]],"hl":null}]},{"m":"put(3, 3) at the front","l":42,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["3:3","1:1"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["1","node"],["3","node"]],"hl":"3"}]},{"m":"get(2) → miss, -1","l":27,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["3:3","1:1"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["1","node"],["3","node"]],"hl":null}]},{"m":"Over capacity → evict least recent key 1","l":42,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["4:4","3:3"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["3","node"],["4","node"]],"hl":null}]},{"m":"put(4, 4) at the front","l":42,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["4:4","3:3"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["3","node"],["4","node"]],"hl":"4"}]},{"m":"get(1) → miss, -1","l":27,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["4:4","3:3"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["3","node"],["4","node"]],"hl":null}]},{"m":"get(3) → 3; move it to the front","l":30,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["3:3","4:4"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["3","node"],["4","node"]],"hl":"3"}]},{"m":"get(4) → 4; move it to the front","l":30,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["4:4","3:3"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["3","node"],["4","node"]],"hl":"4"}]},{"m":"Result: [None, None, 1, None, -1, None, -1, 3, 4]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"recency (most → least)","v":["4:4","3:3"],"p":{},"hl":[0],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"map","n":"map","v":[["3","node"],["4","node"]],"hl":"4"}]}]},"tests":1},"merge-k-sorted-lists":{"statement":"Merge <code>k</code> sorted linked lists into one sorted list.","examples":[["lists = [[1, 4, 5], [1, 3, 4], [2, 6]]","[1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6]"],["lists = []","[]"],["lists = [[]]","[]"]],"vizIn":"lists = [[1, 4, 5], [1, 3, 4], [2, 6]]","brute":{"idea":"Merge the lists one by one into a growing result.","tc":"O(k · N)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def merge_k_lists(lists):\n    def merge(a, b):\n        dummy = t = ListNode()\n        while a and b:\n            if a.val <= b.val:\n                t.next, a = a, a.next\n            else:\n                t.next, b = b, b.next\n            t = t.next\n        t.next = a or b\n        return dummy.next\n    res = None\n    for l in lists:\n        res = merge(res, l)\n    return res"},"opt":{"idea":"Push every list's head into a min-heap. Pop the smallest node, append it, push its next. The heap never holds more than k nodes.","tc":"O(N log k)","sc":"O(k)","code":"def merge_k_lists(lists):\n    import heapq\n    heap = [(node.val, i, node) for i, node in enumerate(lists) if node]\n    heapq.heapify(heap)\n    dummy = tail = ListNode()\n    while heap:\n        val, i, node = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        tail.next = node\n        tail = node\n        if node.next:\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (node.next.val, i, node.next))\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"Pop smallest head 1 (from list 0)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["1","2","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","4","5"],"p":{"tail":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 1 (from list 1)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["2","3","4"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","3","4"],"p":{"tail":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 2 (from list 2)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["3","4","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","6"],"p":{"tail":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 3 (from list 1)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["4","4","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4"],"p":{"tail":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 4 (from list 0)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["4","5","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"tail":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 4 (from list 1)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["5","6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4","4"],"p":{"tail":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 5 (from list 0)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":["6"],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4","4","5"],"p":{"tail":6},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Pop smallest head 6 (from list 2)","l":10,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4","4","5","6"],"p":{"tail":7},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"arr","n":"heap (values)","v":[],"p":{},"hl":[],"ok":[],"bad":[]},{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","1","2","3","4","4","5","6"],"p":{"tail":7},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"reverse-nodes-in-k-group":{"statement":"Reverse the nodes k at a time; a final group shorter than k stays as is.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], k = 2","[2, 1, 4, 3, 5]"],["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], k = 3","[3, 2, 1, 4, 5]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], k = 3","brute":{"idea":"Copy values to an array, reverse each full chunk, rebuild.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def reverse_k_group(head, k):\n    vals = []\n    while head:\n        vals.append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    for i in range(0, len(vals) - len(vals) % k, k):\n        vals[i:i + k] = vals[i:i + k][::-1]\n    return mk_list(vals)"},"opt":{"idea":"For each group: check k nodes exist, reverse them in place, and connect the previous group's tail to the new group head.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def reverse_k_group(head, k):\n    dummy = ListNode(0, head)\n    group_prev = dummy\n    while True:\n        kth = group_prev\n        for _ in range(k):\n            kth = kth.next\n            if not kth:\n                return dummy.next\n        group_next = kth.next\n        prev, cur = group_next, group_prev.next\n        while cur is not group_next:\n            cur.next, prev, cur = prev, cur, cur.next\n        first = group_prev.next\n        group_prev.next = kth\n        group_prev = first","frames":[{"m":"Reversed a group of 3; it now starts with 3","l":15,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","1","4","5","6","7"],"p":{"group_end":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[0]}]},{"m":"Reversed a group of 3; it now starts with 6","l":15,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","1","6","5","4","7"],"p":{"group_end":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]},{"m":"Result: [3, 2, 1, 6, 5, 4, 7]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","2","1","6","5","4","7"],"p":{"group_end":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]}]},"tests":2},"rotate-list":{"statement":"Rotate the list to the right by <code>k</code> places.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], k = 2","[4, 5, 1, 2, 3]"],["head = [0, 1, 2], k = 4","[2, 0, 1]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], k = 2","brute":{"idea":"Move the last node to the front, k times.","tc":"O(n · k)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def rotate_right(head, k):\n    if not head or not head.next:\n        return head\n    for _ in range(k):\n        prev, cur = None, head\n        while cur.next:\n            prev, cur = cur, cur.next\n        prev.next, cur.next, head = None, head, cur\n    return head"},"opt":{"idea":"Find length n and the tail, link tail to head to make a ring, then cut after node n − k % n − 1.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def rotate_right(head, k):\n    if not head:\n        return head\n    n, tail = 1, head\n    while tail.next:\n        n, tail = n + 1, tail.next\n    k %= n\n    if k == 0:\n        return head\n    tail.next = head\n    new_tail = head\n    for _ in range(n - k - 1):\n        new_tail = new_tail.next\n    new_head = new_tail.next\n    new_tail.next = None\n    return new_head","frames":[{"m":"Length 5; link the tail to the head to make a ring","l":10,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"ring","v":["1","2","3","4","5"],"p":{"tail":4},"cyc":0,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Cut after 3; 4 is the new head","l":14,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"rotated","v":["4","5","1","2","3"],"p":{"head":0,"tail":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [4, 5, 1, 2, 3]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"rotated","v":["4","5","1","2","3"],"p":{"head":0,"tail":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":2},"remove-duplicates-from-sorted-list":{"statement":"Delete duplicates from a sorted list so each value appears once.","examples":[["head = [1, 1, 2]","[1, 2]"],["head = [1, 1, 2, 3, 3]","[1, 2, 3]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 1, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4]","brute":{"idea":"Collect unique values and rebuild the list.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def delete_duplicates(head):\n    vals = []\n    while head:\n        if not vals or vals[-1] != head.val:\n            vals.append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    return mk_list(vals)"},"opt":{"idea":"While cur.next has the same value as cur, bypass it.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def delete_duplicates(head):\n    cur = head\n    while cur and cur.next:\n        if cur.next.val == cur.val:\n            cur.next = cur.next.next\n        else:\n            cur = cur.next\n    return head","frames":[{"m":"Next node repeats 1 → bypass it","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","1","2","3","3","3","4"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1]}]},{"m":"Next node repeats 3 → bypass it","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","3","3","4"],"p":{"cur":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]},{"m":"Next node repeats 3 → bypass it","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","3","4"],"p":{"cur":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, 4]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","3","4"],"p":{"cur":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]}]},"tests":2},"odd-even-linked-list":{"statement":"Group the nodes at odd positions first, then the even positions, keeping relative order.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]","[1, 3, 5, 2, 4]"],["head = [2, 1, 3, 5, 6, 4, 7]","[2, 3, 6, 7, 1, 5, 4]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]","brute":{"idea":"Collect values by position parity and rebuild.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def odd_even_list(head):\n    vals, i = [[], []], 0\n    while head:\n        vals[i % 2].append(head.val)\n        head, i = head.next, i + 1\n    return mk_list(vals[0] + vals[1])"},"opt":{"idea":"Build the odd chain and even chain at the same time by skipping every other node, then attach the even chain after the odd tail.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def odd_even_list(head):\n    if not head:\n        return head\n    odd, even = head, head.next\n    even_head = even\n    while even and even.next:\n        odd.next = even.next\n        odd = odd.next\n        even.next = odd.next\n        even = even.next\n    odd.next = even_head\n    return head","frames":[{"m":"Extend both chains by one","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"odd chain","v":["1","3","4","5","6","7"],"p":{"odd":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"even chain","v":["2","4","5","6","7"],"p":{"even":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Extend both chains by one","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"odd chain","v":["1","3","5","6","7"],"p":{"odd":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"even chain","v":["2","4","6","7"],"p":{"even":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Extend both chains by one","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"odd chain","v":["1","3","5","7"],"p":{"odd":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"even chain","v":["2","4","6"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 3, 5, 7, 2, 4, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"odd chain","v":["1","3","5","7"],"p":{"odd":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"even chain","v":["2","4","6"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":2},"sort-list":{"statement":"Sort a linked list in O(n log n) time.","examples":[["head = [4, 2, 1, 3]","[1, 2, 3, 4]"],["head = [-1, 5, 3, 4, 0]","[-1, 0, 3, 4, 5]"],["head = []","[]"]],"vizIn":"head = [5, 2, 7, 1, 3]","brute":{"idea":"Copy values out, sort, write them back.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def sort_list(head):\n    vals = []\n    cur = head\n    while cur:\n        vals.append(cur.val)\n        cur = cur.next\n    return mk_list(sorted(vals))"},"opt":{"idea":"Merge sort: split at the middle with fast/slow, sort each half recursively, merge the two sorted halves.","tc":"O(n log n)","sc":"O(log n) recursion","code":"def sort_list(head):\n    if not head or not head.next:\n        return head\n    slow, fast = head, head.next\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n    right, slow.next = slow.next, None\n    a, b = sort_list(head), sort_list(right)\n    dummy = tail = ListNode()\n    while a and b:\n        if a.val <= b.val:\n            tail.next, a = a, a.next\n        else:\n            tail.next, b = b, b.next\n        tail = tail.next\n    tail.next = a or b\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"Split into two halves","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"left","v":["5","2","7"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"right","v":["1","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Split into two halves","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"left","v":["5","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"right","v":["7"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Split into two halves","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"left","v":["5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"right","v":["2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Merge two sorted halves","l":15,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["2","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Merge two sorted halves","l":15,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["2","5","7"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Split into two halves","l":7,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"left","v":["1"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"right","v":["3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Merge two sorted halves","l":15,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Merge two sorted halves","l":15,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","2","3","5","7"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 3, 5, 7]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"merged","v":["1","2","3","5","7"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":3},"swap-nodes-in-pairs":{"statement":"Swap every two adjacent nodes (change the links, not the values).","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4]","[2, 1, 4, 3]"],["head = []","[]"],["head = [1, 2, 3]","[2, 1, 3]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]","brute":{"idea":"Swap values in place — not allowed by the problem — or rebuild from an array.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def swap_pairs(head):\n    vals = []\n    while head:\n        vals.append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    for i in range(0, len(vals) - 1, 2):\n        vals[i], vals[i + 1] = vals[i + 1], vals[i]\n    return mk_list(vals)"},"opt":{"idea":"With a dummy before the head, for each pair a → b: prev → b, b → a, a → rest. Then prev = a.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def swap_pairs(head):\n    dummy = ListNode(0, head)\n    prev = dummy\n    while prev.next and prev.next.next:\n        a, b = prev.next, prev.next.next\n        prev.next, a.next, b.next = b, b.next, a\n        prev = a\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"Swapped 1 and 2","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["2","1","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"prev":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1,0]}]},{"m":"Swapped 3 and 4","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["2","1","4","3","5","6"],"p":{"prev":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3,2]}]},{"m":"Swapped 5 and 6","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["2","1","4","3","6","5"],"p":{"prev":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[5,4]}]},{"m":"Result: [2, 1, 4, 3, 6, 5]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["2","1","4","3","6","5"],"p":{"prev":5},"cyc":-1,"hl":[5,4]}]}]},"tests":3},"reverse-linked-list-ii":{"statement":"Reverse the nodes from position <code>left</code> to <code>right</code> (1-indexed) in one pass.","examples":[["head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], left = 2, right = 4","[1, 4, 3, 2, 5]"],["head = [5], left = 1, right = 1","[5]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], left = 2, right = 5","brute":{"idea":"Copy values, reverse the slice, rebuild.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def reverse_between(head, left, right):\n    vals = []\n    while head:\n        vals.append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    vals[left - 1:right] = vals[left - 1:right][::-1]\n    return mk_list(vals)"},"opt":{"idea":"Walk to the node before 'left'. Then repeatedly take the node after the current sub-list tail and move it to the front of the sub-list (head insertion), right − left times.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def reverse_between(head, left, right):\n    dummy = ListNode(0, head)\n    before = dummy\n    for _ in range(left - 1):\n        before = before.next\n    cur = before.next\n    for _ in range(right - left):\n        move = cur.next\n        cur.next = move.next\n        move.next = before.next\n        before.next = move\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"Move 3 to the front of the sub-list","l":10,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","3","2","4","5","6"],"p":{"before":0,"cur":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1]}]},{"m":"Move 4 to the front of the sub-list","l":10,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","4","3","2","5","6"],"p":{"before":0,"cur":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1]}]},{"m":"Move 5 to the front of the sub-list","l":10,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","5","4","3","2","6"],"p":{"before":0,"cur":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 5, 4, 3, 2, 6]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","5","4","3","2","6"],"p":{"before":0,"cur":4},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1]}]}]},"tests":2},"partition-list":{"statement":"Put all nodes with value &lt; <code>x</code> before nodes ≥ x, keeping the original order within each part.","examples":[["head = [1, 4, 3, 2, 5, 2], x = 3","[1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 5]"],["head = [2, 1], x = 2","[1, 2]"]],"vizIn":"head = [1, 4, 3, 2, 5, 2], x = 3","brute":{"idea":"Collect the two groups of values and rebuild.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(n)","code":"def partition(head, x):\n    lo, hi = [], []\n    while head:\n        (lo if head.val < x else hi).append(head.val)\n        head = head.next\n    return mk_list(lo + hi)"},"opt":{"idea":"Append each node to a 'less' list or a 'rest' list (each with a dummy head), then join less → rest and cut the tail.","tc":"O(n)","sc":"O(1)","code":"def partition(head, x):\n    less = lt = ListNode()\n    rest = rt = ListNode()\n    while head:\n        if head.val < x:\n            lt.next, lt = head, head\n        else:\n            rt.next, rt = head, head\n        nxt = head.next\n        head.next = None\n        head = nxt\n    lt.next = rest.next\n    return less.next","frames":[{"m":"1 goes to less","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"4 goes to rest","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"3 goes to rest","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"2 goes to less","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4","3"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"5 goes to rest","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4","3","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"2 goes to less","l":9,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1","2","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4","3","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Result: [1, 2, 2, 4, 3, 5]","l":-1,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"less","v":["1","2","2"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4","3","5"],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}]},"tests":2}},"demo":{"code":"def reverse_demo():\n    head = mk_list([1, 2, 3, 4])\n    prev, cur = None, head\n    while cur:\n        nxt = cur.next\n        cur.next = prev\n        prev, cur = cur, nxt\n    return prev","frames":[{"m":"Start: prev = None, cur = head","l":3,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","2","3","4"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed so far","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Flip 1's arrow back, step forward","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["2","3","4"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed so far","v":["1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Flip 2's arrow back, step forward","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["3","4"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed so far","v":["2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Flip 3's arrow back, step forward","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":["4"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed so far","v":["3","2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Flip 4's arrow back, step forward","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"rest","v":[],"p":{},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"list","n":"reversed so far","v":["4","3","2","1"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]}],"title":"Reversing a list in place with prev / cur / nxt"},"lessons":[{"level":"Basics","title":"Nodes and pointers","body":"\n<p>An array keeps items in neighbouring boxes. A <b>linked list</b> keeps each item in its own <b>node</b>, anywhere in memory, and each node stores a <b>pointer</b> (reference) to the next node.</p>\n<div class=\"pic\">head → [3 | •] → [7 | •] → [1 | •] → None\n        val  next</div>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">class ListNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, next=None):\n        self.val = val\n        self.next = next</code></pre>\n<p>You only hold the <code>head</code>. To reach the k-th node you must walk k steps — there is no <code>list[k]</code>. In return, once you hold a node, inserting or removing next to it is O(1): just change arrows, nothing shifts.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">cur = head\nwhile cur:              # the standard walk\n    print(cur.val)\n    cur = cur.next</code></pre>\n","practice":["remove-duplicates-from-sorted-list"],"demo":{"code":"def build_and_walk():\n    vals = [3, 7, 1, 9]\n    head = None\n    for v in reversed(vals):\n        head = ListNode(v, head)\n    cur, total = head, 0\n    while cur:\n        total += cur.val\n        cur = cur.next\n    return total","frames":[{"m":"Create node 9 pointing to the old head","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["9"],"p":{"head":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Create node 1 pointing to the old head","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["1","9"],"p":{"head":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Create node 7 pointing to the old head","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["7","1","9"],"p":{"head":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Create node 3 pointing to the old head","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","7","1","9"],"p":{"head":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"Walk: visit 3, running total 3","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","7","1","9"],"p":{"cur":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["total","3"]]}]},{"m":"Walk: visit 7, running total 10","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","7","1","9"],"p":{"cur":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["total","10"]]}]},{"m":"Walk: visit 1, running total 11","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","7","1","9"],"p":{"cur":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["total","11"]]}]},{"m":"Walk: visit 9, running total 20","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list","v":["3","7","1","9"],"p":{"cur":3},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]},{"k":"vars","v":[["total","20"]]}]}]}},{"level":"Basics","title":"Insert, delete and the dummy head","body":"\n<p>To <b>insert</b> node <code>x</code> after node <code>p</code>: <code>x.next = p.next; p.next = x</code> (order matters — save the rest first).</p>\n<p>To <b>delete</b> the node after <code>p</code>: <code>p.next = p.next.next</code>.</p>\n<p>Both need the node <i>before</i> the target. But the head has no node before it, which forces special cases. The fix is a <b>dummy</b> node placed in front:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">dummy = ListNode(0, head)\nprev = dummy\nwhile prev.next:\n    if prev.next.val == target:\n        prev.next = prev.next.next   # works even if head is deleted\n    else:\n        prev = prev.next\nreturn dummy.next                    # the real (maybe new) head</code></pre>\n<div class=\"tip\">Whenever the head might change — merge, delete, partition, swap — start with a dummy.</div>\n","practice":["remove-nth-node-from-end-of-list","partition-list","swap-nodes-in-pairs"],"demo":{"code":"def dummy_delete():\n    head = mk_list([6, 2, 6, 3, 6])\n    dummy = ListNode(0, head)\n    prev = dummy\n    while prev.next:\n        if prev.next.val == 6:\n            prev.next = prev.next.next\n        else:\n            prev = prev.next\n    return dummy.next","frames":[{"m":"prev.next is 6 → skip it (prev.next = prev.next.next)","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","6","2","6","3","6"],"p":{"prev":0},"cyc":-1,"hl":[1]}]},{"m":"Keep this node, step forward","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","2","6","3","6"],"p":{"prev":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"prev.next is 6 → skip it (prev.next = prev.next.next)","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","2","6","3","6"],"p":{"prev":1},"cyc":-1,"hl":[2]}]},{"m":"Keep this node, step forward","l":8,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","2","3","6"],"p":{"prev":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"prev.next is 6 → skip it (prev.next = prev.next.next)","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (with dummy 0)","v":["0","2","3","6"],"p":{"prev":2},"cyc":-1,"hl":[3]}]}]}},{"level":"Core","title":"Reversing a list","body":"\n<p>Reversal is the most common linked-list operation. Walk the list and point each node <b>backwards</b>. You need three names:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>prev</code> — the already-reversed part (starts as <code>None</code>),</li>\n<li><code>cur</code> — the node being flipped,</li>\n<li><code>nxt</code> — saved before flipping, or the rest of the list is lost.</li>\n</ul>\n<pre><code class=\"py\">prev, cur = None, head\nwhile cur:\n    nxt = cur.next\n    cur.next = prev\n    prev, cur = cur, nxt\nreturn prev</code></pre>\n<p>Reversing a <b>part</b> of the list (positions left..right, or groups of k) is the same loop plus reconnecting the reversed piece to what comes before and after it.</p>\n","practice":["reverse-linked-list","reverse-linked-list-ii","reverse-nodes-in-k-group"]},{"level":"Core","title":"Fast and slow pointers","body":"\n<p>Move <code>slow</code> one step and <code>fast</code> two steps at a time.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Middle</b>: when fast reaches the end, slow is in the middle.</li>\n<li><b>Cycle</b>: if the list loops, fast eventually laps slow and they meet. If fast reaches <code>None</code>, there's no cycle. O(1) memory, unlike a visited set.</li>\n<li><b>Cycle start</b>: after they meet, put one pointer back at head and move both one step at a time — they meet at the cycle's entrance (follows from the distances walked).</li>\n<li><b>n-th from the end</b>: give one pointer an n-step head start, then move both; when the leader hits the end, the follower is n from the end.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"warn\">Always check <code>while fast and fast.next</code> before <code>fast.next.next</code>.</div>\n","practice":["middle-of-the-linked-list","linked-list-cycle","linked-list-cycle-ii","remove-nth-node-from-end-of-list"],"demo":{"code":"def cycle_lesson():\n    head = mk_list([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], 2)\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow, fast = slow.next, fast.next.next\n        if slow is fast:\n            return True\n    return False","frames":[{"m":"slow moves 1, fast moves 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (6 points back to 3)","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":1,"fast":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow moves 1, fast moves 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (6 points back to 3)","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":2,"fast":4},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow moves 1, fast moves 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (6 points back to 3)","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":3,"fast":2},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"slow moves 1, fast moves 2","l":4,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (6 points back to 3)","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":4,"fast":4},"cyc":2,"hl":[]}]},{"m":"They met → the list has a cycle","l":6,"v":[{"k":"list","n":"list (6 points back to 3)","v":["1","2","3","4","5","6"],"p":{"slow":4,"fast":4},"cyc":2,"hl":[4]}]}]}},{"level":"Core","title":"Merging and splitting","body":"\n<ul>\n<li><b>Merge two sorted lists</b>: a dummy and a <code>tail</code>; attach the smaller head each step, then attach whatever remains.</li>\n<li><b>Partition</b>: build two separate chains (less / rest) with two dummies, then join them. Cut the last tail's <code>next</code> to avoid a cycle.</li>\n<li><b>Merge k lists</b>: a min-heap of the current heads, O(N log k).</li>\n<li><b>Sort a list</b>: merge sort — split at the middle with fast/slow, sort both halves, merge. O(n log n) with no random access needed.</li>\n</ul>\n","practice":["merge-two-sorted-lists","partition-list","merge-k-sorted-lists","sort-list","odd-even-linked-list","add-two-numbers"]},{"level":"Advanced","title":"Combining techniques","body":"\n<p>Harder problems chain the basic moves:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Reorder list</b> (L0 → Ln → L1 → Ln−1 …) = find middle + reverse second half + weave the halves.</li>\n<li><b>Palindrome list</b> = find middle + reverse second half + compare.</li>\n<li><b>Rotate by k</b> = find length and tail, link tail to head (ring), cut at the right place.</li>\n<li><b>Intersection of two lists</b> = pointer a walks A then B, pointer b walks B then A; both travel the same distance and meet at the junction.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>LRU cache — the classic design question</h4>\n<p>You need O(1) lookup <i>and</i> O(1) \"move to most recent\" <i>and</i> O(1) \"remove least recent\". A dict gives the lookup; a <b>doubly linked list</b> (each node has <code>prev</code> and <code>next</code>) gives O(1) removal from anywhere. The dict maps key → node; the list is ordered by recency, with sentinel head and tail nodes so there are no edge cases.</p>\n","practice":["reorder-list","palindrome-linked-list","rotate-list","intersection-of-two-linked-lists","lru-cache"]}]};
